    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Logging Provider**\n\nI've decided on Google Cloud Logging as the target. I'll need to integrate its client library directly into `write_structured_log.py` for this integration, and make sure that it's easy to deploy. The core focus now is on defining the precise logging structure to send to GCP, including choosing key-value pairs for different data types.\n\n\n**Defining Log Structure**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on defining the data structure for the logs I'll be sending. The goal is a clean integration with Google Cloud Logging. I've chosen the GCP Logging service and will be using its Python SDK. My current work centers on how to map different data types from the code to the structured log format for optimal querying and analysis. I'm prioritizing ease of deployment and configuration.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789821320734,
          "start": 1789821318045
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a9f39d001EtGoWjP0oBtjGh",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a9ed79001pqFiAq0KP1F70I",
      "session_id": "ses_f46561307ffevy7w97zI9ZvS7j",
      "time_created": 1789821318045,
      "time_updated": 1789821320735
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "12RPYXADP9D9xsqo",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nimport google.cloud.logging\nimport json\n\ndef write_structured_log(log_name: str, message: str, severity: str = \"INFO\", **kwargs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Writes a structured JSON log event to Google Cloud Logging.\n\n    Args:\n        log_name: The name of the log to write to (e.g., \"my-application-log\").\n        message: The main message for the log entry.\n        severity: The severity level of the log entry (e.g., \"INFO\", \"ERROR\", \"DEBUG\").\n        **kwargs: Additional fields to include in the structured log entry.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = google.cloud.logging.Client()\n    logger = client.logger(log_name)\n\n    # Create a structured payload\n    payload = {\n        \"message\": message,\n        \"severity\": severity,\n        **kwargs\n    }\n\n    logger.log_struct(\n        payload,\n        severity=severity\n    )\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example usage:\n    # Ensure you have authenticated with Google Cloud (e.g., `gcloud auth application-default login`)\n    # and enabled the Cloud Logging API for your project.\n    \n    # Simple log\n    write_structured_log(\n        log_name=\"my-app-logs\",\n        message=\"This is a test structured log entry.\",\n        severity=\"INFO\"\n    )\n\n    # Log with additional fields\n    write_structured_log(\n        log_name=\"my-app-logs\",\n        message=\"User login event.\",\n        severity=\"NOTICE\",\n        user_id=\"12345\",\n        ip_address=\"192.168.1.1\",\n        event_type=\"login_success\"\n    )\n\n    # Log an error\n    write_structured_log(\n        log_name=\"my-app-logs\",\n        message=\"An unexpected error occurred during processing.\",\n        severity=\"ERROR\",\n        component=\"data_processor\",\n        error_code=\"DP-500\",\n        trace_id=\"abc-123\"\n    )\n\n    print(\"Structured log entries sent to Google Cloud Logging. Check your project's Cloud Logging console.\")\n",
            "filePath": "write_structured_log.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
